e":"Variable-size sliding window over a string","lc":3},{"id":"longest-repeating-replacement","title":"Longest Repeating Character Replacement","subtitle":"Variable window · invariant len − maxFreq ≤ k","lc":424},{"id":"min-window-substring","title":"Minimum Window Substring","subtitle":"Smallest window of s covering all of t","lc":76},{"id":"permutation-in-string","title":"Permutation in String","subtitle":"Fixed-size window + frequency match","lc":567},{"id":"sliding-window-maximum","title":"Sliding Window Maximum","subtitle":"Monotonic deque · the front is always the window max","lc":239}]},{"id":"stack","title":"Stack","problems":[{"id":"intro","title":"Overview","subtitle":"LIFO · push, pop, and why \"the top\" matters"},{"id":"valid-parentheses","title":"Valid Parentheses","subtitle":"The top is the bracket that must close next","lc":20},{"id":"baseball-game","title":"Baseball Game","subtitle":"Every operation is about the top","lc":682},{"id":"decode-string","title":"Decode String","subtitle":"k[body] with nesting · \"]\" collapses the top","lc":394},{"id":"longest-valid-parentheses","title":"Longest Valid Parentheses","subtitle":"Stack of indices · a base below every run","lc":32},{"id":"monotonic-intro","title":"Monotonic Stack","subtitle":"Keep it sorted · bigger arrivals resolve the waiters"},{"id":"daily-temperatures","title":"Daily Temperatures","subtitle":"Monotonic stack · new days resolve waiting days","lc":739},{"id":"largest-rectangle-histogram","title":"Largest Rectangle in Histogram","subtitle":"Increasing stack · shorter bars close rectangles","lc":84},{"id":"min-stack","title":"Min Stack","subtitle":"O(1) getMin · a twin min-stack","lc":155},{"id":"evaluate-rpn","title":"Evaluate Reverse Polish Notation","subtitle":"Operand stack · postfix evaluation","lc":150}]},{"id":"linked-list","title":"Linked List","problems":[{"id":"intro","title":"Overview","subtitle":"Nodes, next-pointers, and O(1) surgery"},{"id":"reverse-linked-list","title":"Reverse Linked List","subtitle":"Flip every arrow · prev / curr / next","lc":206},{"id":"merge-two-sorted-lists","title":"Merge Two Sorted Lists","subtitle":"Splice the smaller head · dummy node","lc":21},{"id":"add-two-numbers","title":"Add Two Numbers","subtitle":"Elementary addition · carry","lc":2},{"id":"linked-list-cycle","title":"Linked List Cycle","subtitle":"Floyd's tortoise & hare","lc":141},{"id":"palindrome-linked-list","title":"Palindrome Linked List","subtitle":"Middle + reverse half + two pointers","lc":234},{"id":"remove-nth-from-end","title":"Remove Nth Node From End","subtitle":"Two pointers locked n apart","lc":19},{"id":"reorder-list","title":"Reorder List","subtitle":"Middle + reverse + alternate merge","lc":143},{"id":"swap-nodes-in-pairs","title":"Swap Nodes in Pairs","subtitle":"Three arrows per pair · dummy head","lc":24},{"id":"lru-cache","title":"LRU Cache","subtitle":"Hash map + doubly linked list · O(1) get / put","lc":146}]},{"id":"heap","title":"Heap","problems":[{"id":"intro","title":"Overview","subtitle":"Complete tree + heap property · sift-up / sift-down"},{"id":"kth-largest-element","title":"Kth Largest Element in an Array","subtitle":"Min-heap of size k as a top-k gate","lc":215},{"id":"k-closest-points","title":"K Closest Points to Origin","subtitle":"Max-heap of size k, keyed by distance","lc":973},{"id":"find-k-closest-elements","title":"Find K Closest Elements","subtitle":"Max-heap keyed by (distance, value)","lc":658},{"id":"merge-k-sorted-lists","title":"Merge K Sorted Lists","subtitle":"Min-heap of the k current heads","lc":23},{"id":"median-from-data-stream","title":"Median from Data Stream","subtitle":"Two heaps straddling the middle","lc":295},{"id":"task-scheduler","title":"Task Scheduler","subtitle":"Most-frequent-first · max-heap vs. the frame formula","lc":621},{"id":"relative-ranks","title":"Relative Ranks","subtitle":"Sort the indices so the scores keep their owners","lc":506}]},{"id":"binary-search","title":"Binary Search","problems":[{"id":"intro","title":"Overview","subtitle":"Halve the search space · then search answers, not arrays"},{"id":"binary-search","title":"Binary Search","subtitle":"The canonical template · halve [lo, hi]","lc":704},{"id":"search-insert-position","title":"Search Insert Position","subtitle":"Where lo lands when the target is missing","lc":35},{"id":"peak-index-mountain","title":"Peak Index in a Mountain Array","subtitle":"Binary search without a sorted array","lc":852},{"id":"max-candies-k-children","title":"Maximum Candies Allocated to K Children","subtitle":"Binary search the answer, not the array","lc":2226},{"id":"koko-eating-bananas","title":"Apple Harvest (Koko Eating Bananas)","subtitle":"Binary search on the answer · feasibility probe","lc":875},{"id":"search-rotated-sorted","title":"Search in Rotated Sorted Array","subtitle":"One half is always sorted, use it to steer","lc":33},{"id":"find-min-rotated","title":"Find Minimum in Rotated Sorted Array","subtitle":"Compare mid to hi to find the cliff","lc":153},{"id":"search-2d-matrix","title":"Search a 2D Matrix","subtitle":"Treat the grid as one flat sorted array · binary search 0..m·n−1","lc":74},{"id":"split-array-largest-sum","title":"Split Array Largest Sum","subtitle":"Binary search the cap · greedy feasibility","lc":410},{"id":"kth-smallest-sorted-matrix","title":"Kth Smallest in a Sorted Matrix","subtitle":"Binary search on values · count ≤ x probes","lc":378},{"id":"minimum-shipping-capacity","title":"Minimum Shipping Capacity","subtitle":"Ship packages in D days · search the capacity","lc":1011}]},{"id":"dfs","title":"Depth-First Search","problems":[{"id":"introduction","title":"Introduction","subtitle":"Go deep, then backtrack · pre/in/post order"},{"id":"fundamentals","title":"Fundamentals","subtitle":"The recursion template: base case → recurse → combine"},{"id":"return-values","title":"Return Values","subtitle":"Bubbling answers UP with post-order"},{"id":"maximum-depth","title":"Maximum Depth of Binary Tree","subtitle":"Depth = 1 + max(left, right)","lc":104},{"id":"path-sum","title":"Path Sum","subtitle":"Root-to-leaf sum == target · carry the remainder down","lc":112},{"id":"passing-values","title":"Passing Values Down and Up","subtitle":"Parameters go down, returns come up"},{"id":"validate-bst","title":"Validate Binary Search Tree","subtitle":"Carry (low, high) bounds down","lc":98},{"id":"calculate-tilt","title":"Binary Tree Tilt","subtitle":"Post-order: return subtree sums, accumulate |L − R|","lc":563},{"id":"diameter","title":"Diameter of a Binary Tree","subtitle":"Post-order heights, track the widest split","lc":543},{"id":"path-sum-ii","title":"Path Sum II","subtitle":"Backtracking: collect every root-to-leaf path == target","lc":113},{"id":"longest-univalue-path","title":"Longest Univalue Path","subtitle":"Longest chain of equal values","lc":687},{"id":"invert-tree","title":"Invert Binary Tree","subtitle":"Pre-order DFS, swap every node's children","lc":226},{"id":"same-tree","title":"Same Tree","subtitle":"Lockstep pre-order DFS over both trees","lc":100},{"id":"lowest-common-ancestor","title":"Lowest Common Ancestor of a Binary Tree","subtitle":"Post-order DFS, bubble a target up, split point wins","lc":236},{"id":"binary-tree-max-path-sum","title":"Binary Tree Maximum Path Sum","subtitle":"Post-order gains · clamp negative arms","lc":124},{"id":"serialize-deserialize","title":"Serialize and Deserialize Binary Tree","subtitle":"Pre-order with null markers, then rebuild from the stream","lc":297},{"id":"graphs-overview","title":"Graphs Overview","subtitle":"Nodes, edges, and why DFS needs a visited set"},{"id":"adjacency-list","title":"Adjacency List","subtitle":"How to store a graph"},{"id":"copy-graph","title":"Copy Graph","subtitle":"Deep clone with an old→new map","lc":133},{"id":"graph-valid-tree","title":"Graph Valid Tree","subtitle":"Connected + exactly n−1 edges + no cycle","lc":261},{"id":"grid-dfs-overview","title":"Matrices","subtitle":"A grid is a graph · DFS the 4 neighbours"},{"id":"flood-fill","title":"Flood Fill","subtitle":"Recolour a connected region","lc":733},{"id":"number-of-islands","title":"Number of Islands","subtitle":"Count components, sink each island","lc":200},{"id":"surrounded-regions","title":"Surrounded Regions","subtitle":"Border-connected O's are safe","lc":130},{"id":"pacific-atlantic","title":"Pacific Atlantic Water Flow","subtitle":"Flood inward from both oceans, intersect","lc":417}]},{"id":"greedy","title":"Greedy Algorithms","problems":[{"id":"overview","title":"Overview","subtitle":"Take the best local choice, never look back"},{"id":"best-time-buy-sell-stock","title":"Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock","subtitle":"Track the cheapest day seen so far","lc":121},{"id":"gas-station","title":"Gas Station","subtitle":"If total gas ≥ total cost, one start works, find it","lc":134},{"id":"jump-game","title":"Jump Game","subtitle":"Track the farthest index you can reach","lc":55},{"id":"jump-game-ii","title":"Jump Game II","subtitle":"Minimum jumps, greedy BFS by levels","lc":45},{"id":"partition-labels","title":"Partition Labels","subtitle":"Extend the part to each letter’s last occurrence","lc":763}]},{"id":"dp","title":"Dynamic Programming","problems":[{"id":"fundamentals","title":"Fundamentals","subtitle":"Overlapping subproblems · a table you fill once"},{"id":"solving-with-dp","title":"Solving a Question with Dynamic Programming","subtitle":"State → recurrence → base case → order → answer"},{"id":"pascals-triangle","title":"Pascal's Triangle","subtitle":"The smallest recurrence there is","lc":118},{"id":"climbing-stairs","title":"Climbing Stairs","subtitle":"ways(i) = ways(i−1) + ways(i−2) · Fibonacci","lc":70},{"id":"dice-combinations","title":"Dice Combinations","subtitle":"dp[i] = Σ dp[i−j] for j in 1..6 · a 6-wide window","lc":377},{"id":"max-subarray","title":"Maximum Subarray","subtitle":"cur = max(nums[i], cur + nums[i]) · Kadane's","lc":53},{"id":"house-robber","title":"House Robber","subtitle":"dp[i] = max(dp[i−1], dp[i−2] + nums[i])","lc":198},{"id":"coin-change","title":"Coin Change","subtitle":"dp[a] = 1 + min(dp[a − coin]) · fewest coins to make amount","lc":322},{"id":"longest-common-subsequence","title":"Longest Common Subsequence","subtitle":"Grid DP · match → diagonal+1, else max(up, left)","lc":1143},{"id":"edit-distance","title":"Edit Distance","subtitle":"Grid DP · dp[i][j] = min edits word1[:i] → word2[:j]","lc":72},{"id":"counting-bits","title":"Counting Bits","subtitle":"dp[i] = dp[i>>1] + (i & 1)","lc":338},{"id":"decode-ways","title":"Decode Ways","subtitle":"1 or 2 digits at a time","lc":91},{"id":"unique-paths","title":"Unique Paths","subtitle":"Grid DP · dp[i][j] = dp[i−1][j] + dp[i][j−1]","lc":62},{"id":"maximal-square","title":"Maximal Square","subtitle":"Grid DP · dp[i][j] = min(up, left, diag) + 1","lc":221},{"id":"longest-increasing-subsequence","title":"Longest Increasing Subsequence","subtitle":"dp[i] = longest increasing run ENDING at i","lc":300},{"id":"word-break","title":"Word Break","subtitle":"dp[i] = can s[0..i) be split into dictionary words","lc":139},{"id":"maximum-profit-job-scheduling","title":"Maximum Profit in Job Scheduling","subtitle":"Sort by end; take or skip","lc":1235},{"id":"paint-house","title":"Paint House","subtitle":"Grid DP · dp[i][c] = cost + min(other two colours)","lc":256},{"id":"paint-house-ii","title":"Paint House II","subtitle":"k colours · track the two smallest → O(n·k)","lc":265},{"id":"minimum-window-subsequence","title":"Minimum Window Subsequence","subtitle":"Smallest window of S containing T as a subsequence","lc":727}]},{"id":"graphs","title":"Graphs","problems":[{"id":"graphs-overview","title":"Overview","subtitle":"Directed, weighted, and how we store them"},{"id":"course-schedule","title":"Course Schedule","subtitle":"Can you finish? = is it a DAG (no cycle)?","lc":207},{"id":"course-schedule-ii","title":"Course Schedule II","subtitle":"Return a valid topological order","lc":210},{"id":"shortest-path-algorithms","title":"Shortest Path Algorithms","subtitle":"BFS vs Dijkstra vs Bellman-Ford"},{"id":"network-delay-time","title":"Network Delay Time","subtitle":"Dijkstra · finalize the nearest unfinished node","lc":743},{"id":"cheapest-flights","title":"Cheapest Flights Within K Stops","subtitle":"Bellman-Ford bounded to K+1 hops","lc":787},{"id":"path-minimum-effort","title":"Path With Minimum Effort","subtitle":"Dijkstra on a grid · minimize the max step","lc":1631},{"id":"find-the-city","title":"Find the City With Fewest Reachable","subtitle":"Floyd-Warshall all-pairs, then count","lc":1334},{"id":"union-find","title":"Union-Find (DSU)","subtitle":"Disjoint sets · find + union"},{"id":"connected-components","title":"Number of Connected Components","subtitle":"Union-Find · count = n, merge drops count","lc":323},{"id":"redundant-connection","title":"Redundant Connection","subtitle":"Union-Find · first cycle-closing edge","lc":684},{"id":"word-ladder","title":"Word Ladder","subtitle":"Shortest transformation sequence via BFS","lc":127}]},{"id":"backtracking","title":"Backtracking","problems":[{"id":"overview","title":"Overview","subtitle":"Choose → explore → un-choose"},{"id":"word-search","title":"Word Search","subtitle":"DFS with mark-and-unmark backtracking","lc":79},{"id":"solution-space-trees","title":"Solution Space Trees","subtitle":"Nodes = partial solutions, edges = choices"},{"id":"subsets","title":"Subsets","subtitle":"Every node of the tree is a subset","lc":78},{"id":"permutations","title":"Permutations","subtitle":"Choose an unused element at each level","lc":46},{"id":"letter-combinations","title":"Letter Combinations of a Phone Number","subtitle":"One digit per tree level","lc":17},{"id":"generate-parentheses","title":"Generate Parentheses","subtitle":"Add '(' or ')' with validity pruning","lc":22},{"id":"combination-sum","title":"Combination Sum","subtitle":"Reuse allowed; prune when the sum overshoots","lc":39},{"id":"palindrome-partitioning","title":"Palindrome Partitioning","subtitle":"Cut only where the prefix is a palindrome","lc":131},{"id":"n-queens","title":"N-Queens","subtitle":"Place row by row, backtrack on attack","lc":51}]},{"id":"bfs","title":"Breadth-First Search","problems":[{"id":"introduction","title":"Introduction","subtitle":"Level by level with a FIFO queue"},{"id":"overview","title":"Overview","subtitle":"Process one whole level per iteration"},{"id":"level-order-sum","title":"Level Order Sum","subtitle":"Sum each level with the level-batching loop","lc":1161},{"id":"rightmost-node","title":"Rightmost Node","subtitle":"Right-side view = last node of each level","lc":199},{"id":"zigzag-level-order","title":"Zigzag Level Order","subtitle":"Alternate L→R, R→L each level","lc":103},{"id":"maximum-width","title":"Maximum Width of Binary Tree","subtitle":"Index nodes by position 2i, 2i+1","lc":662},{"id":"graphs-overview","title":"Graphs Overview","subtitle":"BFS finds the shortest path (fewest edges)"},{"id":"minimum-knight-moves","title":"Minimum Knight Moves","subtitle":"BFS = shortest path on the move-graph","lc":1197},{"id":"rotting-oranges","title":"Rotting Oranges","subtitle":"Multi-source BFS · rot spreads one ring per minute","lc":994},{"id":"01-matrix","title":"01 Matrix","subtitle":"Distance to nearest 0 · multi-source BFS","lc":542},{"id":"bus-routes","title":"Bus Routes","subtitle":"BFS over routes: each level = one more bus","lc":815}]},{"id":"trie","title":"Trie","problems":[{"id":"intro","title":"Overview","subtitle":"Prefix tree · shared prefixes stored once"},{"id":"implement-trie","title":"Implement Trie Methods","subtitle":"insert · search · startsWith","lc":208},{"id":"prefix-matching","title":"Prefix Matching","subtitle":"Autocomplete · walk prefix, collect subtree","lc":1268}]},{"id":"prefix-sum","title":"Prefix Sum","problems":[{"id":"intro","title":"Overview","subtitle":"Precompute running totals · range sum in O(1)"},{"id":"count-vowels-substrings","title":"Count Vowels in Substrings","subtitle":"Prefix-sum a 0/1 indicator"},{"id":"subarray-sum-equals-k","title":"Subarray Sum Equals K","subtitle":"Running prefix + a count hashmap","lc":560}]},{"id":"matrices","title":"Matrices","problems":[{"id":"spiral-matrix","title":"Spiral Matrix","subtitle":"Four shrinking boundaries","lc":54},{"id":"rotate-image","title":"Rotate Image","subtitle":"90° in place · transpose+reverse or 4-cycles","lc":48},{"id":"set-matrix-zeroes","title":"Set Matrix Zeroes","subtitle":"Find then zero · markers in the first row/col","lc":73},{"id":"island-perimeter","title":"Island Perimeter","subtitle":"Count contributions, not the outline","lc":463},{"id":"missing-and-repeated","title":"Find Missing and Repeated Values","subtitle":"Two equations, two unknowns","lc":2965}]},{"id":"intervals","title":"Intervals","problems":[{"id":"overview","title":"Overview","subtitle":"Sort, then sweep · overlap ⇔ b.start ≤ a.end"},{"id":"merge-intervals","title":"Merge Intervals","subtitle":"Sort by start · extend while overlapping","lc":56},{"id":"insert-interval","title":"Insert Interval","subtitle":"Sorted list · three-phase sweep · no sort","lc":57},{"id":"non-overlapping-intervals","title":"Non-overlapping Intervals","subtitle":"Sort by end · greedily keep early finishers","lc":435},{"id":"meeting-rooms","title":"Meeting Rooms","subtitle":"Sort by start · check neighbours overlap","lc":252},{"id":"meeting-rooms-ii","title":"Meeting Rooms II","subtitle":"Chronological sweep · peak overlap = rooms","lc":253}]},{"id":"bit-manipulation","title":"Bit Manipulation","problems":[{"id":"overview","title":"Overview","subtitle":"AND · OR · XOR · shifts · the classic tricks"},{"id":"single-number","title":"Single Number","subtitle":"XOR fold · pairs cancel","lc":136},{"id":"number-of-1-bits","title":"Number of 1 Bits","subtitle":"Hamming weight · n & (n − 1)","lc":191},{"id":"missing-number","title":"Missing Number","subtitle":"XOR index ⊕ value · pairs cancel","lc":268},{"id":"reverse-bits","title":"Reverse Bits","subtitle":"build the answer bit by bit","lc":190},{"id":"sum-of-two-integers","title":"Sum of Two Integers","subtitle":"XOR sum + carry · add without +","lc":371}]}],"activePattern":"two-pointers","activeProblem":"sort-colors"}],"$L19"]}]
1a:I[28440,["2619","static/chunks/2619-04bc32f026a0d946.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","6489","static/chunks/6489-699922ea493f9867.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","1356","static/chunks/1356-9e2757ba007ad1f9.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","951","static/chunks/951-3dbda3a86d4c6444.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","2799","static/chunks/2799-ce430b82b11995d5.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","6589","static/chunks/6589-cfdc115b042e146b.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","3650","static/chunks/3650-106e80ed926f59bf.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","8440","static/chunks/8440-bfb72547be677d52.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","134","static/chunks/app/%5Bpattern%5D/%5BproblemId%5D/page-f9e02a54f5641ad9.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs"],"AnimationRunner"]
19:["$","$L1a","sort-colors",{"problem":{"id":"sort-colors","patternId":"two-pointers","title":"Sort Colors","subtitle":"Dutch National Flag · in-place · three pointers","kind":"problem","leetcode":{"id":75,"slug":"sort-colors","difficulty":"Medium"},"companies":["Microsoft","Amazon","Meta"],"statement":"Given an array of objects colored 0, 1, or 2, sort them in place so equal colors are grouped in that order, ideally in a single pass.","input":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"colorByValue":{"0":{"bg":"#fbe2e2","border":"#c84a4a","text":"#7a1f1f"},"1":{"bg":"#fffdf6","border":"#6a6a6a","text":"#1f1f1f"},"2":{"bg":"#dde7f5","border":"#3a78c2","text":"#1f3f7a"}},"approaches":[{"label":"Brute force · counting sort (two passes)","complexity":{"time":"O(n)","space":"O(1)"},"pseudocode":["given arr","count ← [0, 0, 0]","for v in arr: count[v]++","write count[0] zeros, then count[1] ones, then count[2] twos","return arr"],"steps":[{"codeLine":1,"narration":"Sort an array of 0 (red), 1 (white), 2 (blue), in place. Value-set is tiny, so first idea: counting sort.","vars":[["n",7]]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"count[] of size 3, count[v] = how many times value v appears.","vars":[["phase","pass 1: count"]],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[0,0,0]}},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1, i = 0: arr[i] = 2. count[2]++ → 1.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":0,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[0],"vars":[["i",0],["arr[i]",2]],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[0,0,1],"highlights":[2]}},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1, i = 1: arr[i] = 0. count[0]++ → 1.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":1,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[1],"vars":[["i",1],["arr[i]",0]],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[1,0,1],"highlights":[0]}},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1, i = 2: arr[i] = 1. count[1]++ → 1.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":2,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[2],"vars":[["i",2],["arr[i]",1]],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[1,1,1],"highlights":[1]}},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1, i = 3: arr[i] = 0. count[0]++ → 2.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":3,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[3],"vars":[["i",3],["arr[i]",0]],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[2,1,1],"highlights":[0]}},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1, i = 4: arr[i] = 1. count[1]++ → 2.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":4,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[4],"vars":[["i",4],["arr[i]",1]],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[2,2,1],"highlights":[1]}},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1, i = 5: arr[i] = 2. count[2]++ → 2.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":5,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[5],"vars":[["i",5],["arr[i]",2]],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[2,2,2],"highlights":[2]}},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1, i = 6: arr[i] = 0. count[0]++ → 3.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":6,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[6],"vars":[["i",6],["arr[i]",0]],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[3,2,2],"highlights":[0]}},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1 done. 3 reds, 2 whites, 2 blues.","vars":[["phase","pass 1 → 2"]],"aux":{"label":"count[] (final)","values":[3,2,2],"highlights":[0,1,2]}},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Pass 2: paint the array in place, first count[0] reds, then count[1] whites, then count[2] blues. Left-to-right.","vars":[["phase","pass 2: paint"]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"dimmed":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[3,2,2]}},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Paint red at index 0  (1 of 3).","vars":[["write",0],["value",0]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,0],"pointers":[{"name":"write","index":1,"color":"accent"}],"highlights":[0],"dimmed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[3,2,2],"highlights":[0]}},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Paint red at index 1  (2 of 3).","vars":[["write",1],["value",0]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,0],"pointers":[{"name":"write","index":2,"color":"accent"}],"highlights":[1],"dimmed":[2,3,4,5,6],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[3,2,2],"highlights":[0]}},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Paint red at index 2  (3 of 3).","vars":[["write",2],["value",0]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,0,1,2,0],"pointers":[{"name":"write","index":3,"color":"accent"}],"highlights":[2],"dimmed":[3,4,5,6],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[3,2,2],"highlights":[0]}},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Paint white at index 3  (1 of 2).","vars":[["write",3],["value",1]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,0],"pointers":[{"name":"write","index":4,"color":"accent"}],"highlights":[3],"dimmed":[4,5,6],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[3,2,2],"highlights":[1]}},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Paint white at index 4  (2 of 2).","vars":[["write",4],["value",1]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,0],"pointers":[{"name":"write","index":5,"color":"accent"}],"highlights":[4],"dimmed":[5,6],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[3,2,2],"highlights":[1]}},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Paint blue at index 5  (1 of 2).","vars":[["write",5],["value",2]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,0],"pointers":[{"name":"write","index":6,"color":"accent"}],"highlights":[5],"dimmed":[6],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[3,2,2],"highlights":[2]}},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Paint blue at index 6  (2 of 2).","vars":[["write",6],["value",2]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"pointers":[{"name":"write","index":6,"color":"accent"}],"highlights":[6],"dimmed":[],"aux":{"label":"count[]","values":[3,2,2],"highlights":[2]}},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"Done. O(n) time, O(1) space, but it took TWO passes and rewrote every cell. Can we do it in ONE pass with only swaps?","vars":[["time","O(n)"],["space","O(1)"],["passes",2]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"highlights":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6]}]},{"label":"Better · two-pass swap partition (in place)","complexity":{"time":"O(n)","space":"O(1)"},"pseudocode":["given arr","write ← 0                            // pass 1: 0s → front","for i ← 0 to n − 1:","    if arr[i] == 0:","        swap(arr[write], arr[i]); write++","// 0s settled at [0, write)","back ← n − 1;  i ← write             // pass 2: 2s → back","while i ≤ back:","    if arr[i] == 2:","        swap(arr[i], arr[back]); back−−","    else:                              // arr[i] == 1","        i++","return arr"],"steps":[{"codeLine":1,"narration":"Better idea: same-direction two pointers (the Move Zeroes trick), applied TWICE. Pass 1 sweeps every 0 to the front. Pass 2 sweeps every 2 to the back. The 1s settle into the middle for free. All swaps, no extra memory.","vars":[["n",7],["plan","2 passes, in place"]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t0","t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"Pass 1: write ← 0. The slot `write` is where the next 0 we discover will go. Everything strictly left of `write` is already a settled 0.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":0,"color":"accent"}],"vars":[["phase","pass 1: 0s → front"],["write",0]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t0","t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1: i = 0. Start the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":0,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":0,"color":"ink"}],"vars":[["write",0],["i",0]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t0","t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"arr[i] = 2 (blue), not a 0, so the if fails. Leave it alone, i continues.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":0,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":0,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[0],"vars":[["write",0],["i",0],["arr[i]",2]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t0","t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1: i = 1. Start the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":0,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":1,"color":"ink"}],"vars":[["write",0],["i",1]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t0","t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"arr[i] = 0 (red) → swap arr[write] ↔ arr[i]. The red 0 slides left to slot write; whatever non-zero was sitting at write slides right to position i (we don't care about its order yet, pass 2 will fix it).","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":0,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":1,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[0,1],"vars":[["write",0],["i",1]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t0","t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"Swap done, the red and the non-zero slid past each other. write++ → 1. The 0-region grew by one red on the left.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":1,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":1,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[0],"vars":[["write",1],["i",1]],"arrValues":[0,2,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t0","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":1,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1: i = 2. Start the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":1,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":2,"color":"ink"}],"vars":[["write",1],["i",2]],"arrValues":[0,2,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t0","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":1,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"arr[i] = 1 (white), not a 0, so the if fails. Leave it alone, i continues.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":1,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":2,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[2],"vars":[["write",1],["i",2],["arr[i]",1]],"arrValues":[0,2,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t0","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":1,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1: i = 3. Start the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":1,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":3,"color":"ink"}],"vars":[["write",1],["i",3]],"arrValues":[0,2,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t0","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":1,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"arr[i] = 0 (red) → swap arr[write] ↔ arr[i]. The red 0 slides left to slot write; whatever non-zero was sitting at write slides right to position i (we don't care about its order yet, pass 2 will fix it).","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":1,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":3,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[1,3],"vars":[["write",1],["i",3]],"arrValues":[0,2,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t0","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":1,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"Swap done, the red and the non-zero slid past each other. write++ → 2. The 0-region grew by one red on the left.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":3,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[1],"vars":[["write",2],["i",3]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,2,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t2","t0","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1: i = 4. Start the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":4,"color":"ink"}],"vars":[["write",2],["i",4]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,2,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t2","t0","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"arr[i] = 1 (white), not a 0, so the if fails. Leave it alone, i continues.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":4,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[4],"vars":[["write",2],["i",4],["arr[i]",1]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,2,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t2","t0","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1: i = 5. Start the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":5,"color":"ink"}],"vars":[["write",2],["i",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,2,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t2","t0","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"arr[i] = 2 (blue), not a 0, so the if fails. Leave it alone, i continues.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":5,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[5],"vars":[["write",2],["i",5],["arr[i]",2]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,2,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t2","t0","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Pass 1: i = 6. Start the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":6,"color":"ink"}],"vars":[["write",2],["i",6]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,2,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t2","t0","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"arr[i] = 0 (red) → swap arr[write] ↔ arr[i]. The red 0 slides left to slot write; whatever non-zero was sitting at write slides right to position i (we don't care about its order yet, pass 2 will fix it).","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":6,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[2,6],"vars":[["write",2],["i",6]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,2,1,2,0],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t2","t0","t4","t5","t6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"Swap done, the red and the non-zero slid past each other. write++ → 3. The 0-region grew by one red on the left.","pointers":[{"name":"write","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"i","index":6,"color":"ink"}],"highlights":[2],"vars":[["write",3],["i",6]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,2,1,2,1],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t0","t4","t5","t2"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":6,"narration":"Pass 1 done. The first 3 cells are settled 0s. The remaining 4 cells contain only 1s and 2s, in some order, pass 2 will sort them.","vars":[["phase","pass 1 → 2"],["write (final)",3]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,2,1,2,1],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t0","t4","t5","t2"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"non-zeros (1s + 2s, mixed)"}]},{"codeLine":7,"narration":"Pass 2: same trick for 2s, but mirrored. i ← 3 (where the 0s end); back ← n − 1 = 6. Now we walk inward, when we see a 2, swap it with arr[back] and shrink back.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":6,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["phase","pass 2: 2s → back"],["i",3],["back",6]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,2,1,2,1],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t0","t4","t5","t2"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":3,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":7,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":8,"narration":"i (3) ≤ back (6), pass 2 loop continues.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":6,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["i",3],["back",6]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,2,1,2,1],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t0","t4","t5","t2"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":3,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":7,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":10,"narration":"arr[i] = 2 (blue) → swap arr[i] ↔ arr[back]. The blue slides right; an unknown cell from arr[back] slides to i. i stays, we must re-examine the cell that just arrived (same gotcha as Dutch flag).","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":6,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[3,6],"vars":[["i",3],["back",6]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,2,1,2,1],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t0","t4","t5","t2"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":3,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":7,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":10,"narration":"Swap done. back−− → 5. The 2-region grew by one blue on the right; an unknown value waits at i = 3 (currently 1 = white), examine it next.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[6],"vars":[["i",3],["back",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":3,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":8,"narration":"i (3) ≤ back (5), pass 2 loop continues.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["i",3],["back",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":3,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":11,"narration":"arr[i] = 1 (white), already in the 1-region. Just advance i.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[3],"vars":[["i",3],["back",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":3,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":12,"narration":"i++ → 4. The 1-region is now [3 … 4).","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":4,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[3],"vars":[["i",4],["back",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":4,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":4,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":8,"narration":"i (4) ≤ back (5), pass 2 loop continues.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":4,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["i",4],["back",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":4,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":4,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":11,"narration":"arr[i] = 1 (white), already in the 1-region. Just advance i.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":4,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[4],"vars":[["i",4],["back",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":4,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":4,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":12,"narration":"i++ → 5. The 1-region is now [3 … 5).","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":5,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[4],"vars":[["i",5],["back",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":8,"narration":"i (5) ≤ back (5), pass 2 loop continues.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":5,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["i",5],["back",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":10,"narration":"arr[i] = 2 (blue) → swap arr[i] ↔ arr[back]. i == back, so swap with self, no-op, but back will still contract, settling this blue. Loop will exit right after.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":5,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[5,5],"vars":[["i",5],["back",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":10,"narration":"Fold-in done. back−− → 4. The 2-region grew by one blue.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":5,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":4,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[5],"vars":[["i",5],["back",4]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":5,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":5,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":8,"narration":"i (5) > back (4), pass 2 done.","pointers":[{"name":"i","index":5,"color":"accent"},{"name":"back","index":4,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["i",5],["back",4]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":5,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":5,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":13,"narration":"Done, reds, whites, blues, all sorted. O(n) time, O(1) space, no extra memory. But we walked the array TWICE: pass 1 partitioned 0s vs non-0s, pass 2 partitioned 1s vs 2s. The two passes are doing similar work at opposite ends. Could we run BOTH partitions in a single walk?","vars":[["time","O(n)"],["space","O(1)"],["passes",2]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["t1","t3","t6","t2","t4","t5","t0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (from pass 1)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":5,"tint":"gray","label":"mixed 1s / 2s"},{"start":5,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]}]},{"label":"Optimized · Dutch National Flag (in place, one pass)","complexity":{"time":"O(n)","space":"O(1)"},"pseudocode":["low ← 0; mid ← 0; high ← n − 1","while mid ≤ high:","    if arr[mid] == 0:","        swap(arr[low], arr[mid]); low++; mid++","    else if arr[mid] == 1:","        mid++","    else:                          // arr[mid] == 2","        swap(arr[mid], arr[high]); high−−","return arr"],"steps":[{"codeLine":1,"narration":"Dutch National Flag, fuse BOTH passes from the previous approach into a single walk. Use THREE pointers: low (where 0s end, like pass 1's `write`), mid (the scanner), high (where 2s begin, like pass 2's `back`). One walk, in place.","vars":[["n",7]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["c0","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]},{"codeLine":1,"narration":"Invariant we maintain every step: cells STRICTLY LEFT of `low` are all 0s · between [low … mid) are all 1s · between [mid … high] is unprocessed (mid scans this) · STRICTLY RIGHT of `high` are all 2s.","arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["c0","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]},{"codeLine":1,"narration":"Initialize low ← 0, mid ← 0, high ← n − 1. All settled regions on the left and right are empty; the entire array is unprocessed.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":0,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":0,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":6,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["low",0],["mid",0],["high",6]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["c0","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":7,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"Iter 1: mid (0) ≤ high (6), the unprocessed window is non-empty, enter the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":0,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":0,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":6,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["low",0],["mid",0],["high",6]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["c0","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":7,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":7,"narration":"arr[mid] = 2 (blue) → belongs at the right end. Swap arr[mid] ↔ arr[high], then high−−. CRUCIAL: mid does NOT advance. The cell sliding in from arr[high] is from the UNPROCESSED window, we have no idea what color it is. We must re-examine arr[mid] next step.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":0,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":0,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":6,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[0,6],"vars":[["low",0],["mid",0],["high",6],["arr[mid]",2],["arr[high]",0]],"arrValues":[2,0,1,0,1,2,0],"arrIds":["c0","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":7,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":7,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":8,"narration":"Swap done, the blue slid right, an unknown cell slid left. high−− → 5. mid stays at 0; the value now waiting there is arr[0] = 0 (red), classify it next.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":0,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":0,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[6],"vars":[["low",0],["mid",0],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"Iter 2: mid (0) ≤ high (5), the unprocessed window is non-empty, enter the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":0,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":0,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["low",0],["mid",0],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"arr[mid] = 0 (red) → belongs in the 0-region. Swap arr[low] ↔ arr[mid]. Here low == mid, so this is swapping a cell with itself, a no-op. We just fold this red cell into the growing 0-region.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":0,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":0,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[0,0],"vars":[["low",0],["mid",0],["high",5],["arr[low]",0],["arr[mid]",0]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":0,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":0,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Fold-in done. low++ → 1, mid++ → 1. The 0-region grew by one red cell on the left.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":1,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":1,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[0],"vars":[["low",1],["mid",1],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":1,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":1,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"Iter 3: mid (1) ≤ high (5), the unprocessed window is non-empty, enter the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":1,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":1,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["low",1],["mid",1],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":1,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":1,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"arr[mid] = 0 (red) → belongs in the 0-region. Swap arr[low] ↔ arr[mid]. Here low == mid, so this is swapping a cell with itself, a no-op. We just fold this red cell into the growing 0-region.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":1,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":1,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[1,1],"vars":[["low",1],["mid",1],["high",5],["arr[low]",0],["arr[mid]",0]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":1,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":1,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":1,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Fold-in done. low++ → 2, mid++ → 2. The 0-region grew by one red cell on the left.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":2,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[1],"vars":[["low",2],["mid",2],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":2,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"Iter 4: mid (2) ≤ high (5), the unprocessed window is non-empty, enter the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":2,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["low",2],["mid",2],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":2,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"arr[mid] = 1 (white) → it is ALREADY in the right place. The 1-region is [low … mid); advancing mid extends that boundary to swallow this white cell. No swap needed.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":2,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[2],"vars":[["low",2],["mid",2],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":2,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":6,"narration":"mid++ → 3. The 1-region is now [2 … 3).","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":3,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[2],"vars":[["low",2],["mid",3],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":3,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"Iter 5: mid (3) ≤ high (5), the unprocessed window is non-empty, enter the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":3,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["low",2],["mid",3],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":3,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"arr[mid] = 0 (red) → belongs in the 0-region. Swap arr[low] ↔ arr[mid]. Why this is safe: arr[low] sits inside the 1-region [low … mid), so it MUST be a white 1. The swap drops the red 0 at low and pushes the displaced white 1 to mid, watch the cells slide.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":2,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":3,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[2,3],"vars":[["low",2],["mid",3],["high",5],["arr[low]",1],["arr[mid]",0]],"arrValues":[0,0,1,0,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":2,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":2,"end":3,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"Swap done, the red and white cells slid past each other. low++ → 3, mid++ → 4. The 0-region grew by one red on the left; the 1-region also slid right, keeping its size.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":4,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[2],"vars":[["low",3],["mid",4],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c3","c2","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":4,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":4,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"Iter 6: mid (4) ≤ high (5), the unprocessed window is non-empty, enter the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":4,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["low",3],["mid",4],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c3","c2","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":4,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":4,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"arr[mid] = 1 (white) → it is ALREADY in the right place. The 1-region is [low … mid); advancing mid extends that boundary to swallow this white cell. No swap needed.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":4,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[4],"vars":[["low",3],["mid",4],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c3","c2","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":4,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":4,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":6,"narration":"mid++ → 5. The 1-region is now [3 … 5).","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":5,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[4],"vars":[["low",3],["mid",5],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c3","c2","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"Iter 7: mid (5) ≤ high (5), the unprocessed window is non-empty, enter the loop body.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":5,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["low",3],["mid",5],["high",5]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c3","c2","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":7,"narration":"arr[mid] = 2 (blue) → belongs in the 2-region. Swap arr[mid] ↔ arr[high]. Here mid == high, swap with self is a no-op, but high will still contract, settling this blue. The loop will exit right after.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":5,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":5,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[5,5],"vars":[["low",3],["mid",5],["high",5],["arr[mid]",2],["arr[high]",2]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c3","c2","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":6,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":6,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":8,"narration":"Fold-in done. high−− → 4. The 2-region grew by one blue.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":5,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":4,"color":"accent2"}],"highlights":[5],"vars":[["low",3],["mid",5],["high",4]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c3","c2","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":5,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":5,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"mid (5) > high (4), the unprocessed window is empty. Loop exits.","pointers":[{"name":"low","index":3,"color":"accent"},{"name":"mid","index":5,"color":"ink"},{"name":"high","index":4,"color":"accent2"}],"vars":[["low",3],["mid",5],["high",4]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c3","c2","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":5,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":5,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]},{"codeLine":9,"narration":"Done. Every cell sits in its correct region, reds, whites, blues, left to right. ONE pass through the array. O(n) time, O(1) extra space.","vars":[["time","O(n)"],["space","O(1)"],["passes",1]],"arrValues":[0,0,0,1,1,2,2],"arrIds":["c6","c1","c3","c2","c4","c5","c0"],"regions":[{"start":0,"end":3,"tint":"red","label":"0-region (settled)"},{"start":3,"end":5,"tint":"neutral","label":"1-region (settled)"},{"start":5,"end":5,"tint":"gray","label":"unprocessed"},{"start":5,"end":7,"tint":"blue","label":"2-region (settled)"}]}]}]},"patternTitle":"Two Pointers"}]
